  "articleBody": "A garage remodel can be a fantastic way to add functionality and value to your home, but it's easy to stumble if you're not careful. One of the biggest mistakes we see is starting without a clear plan. It's crucial to define what you want to use the space for before you even pick up a hammer. Another common pitfall is underestimating the budget. Costs can add up quickly, especially if unexpected issues pop up, so always factor in a contingency. Choosing poor flooring or materials is another one – your garage takes a lot of abuse, so invest in durable options that can withstand spills, heavy traffic, and temperature changes. And please, don't take on work without the right skills or tools! If your project involves structural changes, electrical work, or plumbing, trying to DIY it can lead to safety hazards and costly redo's. When you're ready for a significant transformation, calling in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC, who handles everything from framing to drywall in areas like Highlands Ranch and Thornton, can save you a lot of headaches and ensure a high-quality finish.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}